comctl32_v6, user32: the press that drops a combo list never picks an item; closing without a pick restores the selection, as on Windows
(neutron combo-handover, revision 4 -- replaces cbx186's combo-handover.mypatch and cbx187's revisions 2 and 3; kill switches
NEUTRON_COMBO_HANDOVER=0 (press / hand-over / coordinates) and NEUTRON_COMBO_ESCAPE_RESTORE=0 (Escape, CB_SHOWDROPDOWN); stacks on
popup-input-anchor)

What he saw (runtime 11.10-186, Photoshop 2026, KDE Plasma Wayland, 175%): Edit > Color Settings > RGB working space: "it lists
them but it's broken as fuck. It closes instantly after you click it and it changes the color space. You have to hold the click
to keep it up. That's pretty bad". His call (C233): revise the combo fix to Windows' rule.

Mechanism (SOLID, lab message logs). The press on the combo drops the list and the combo keeps the capture; once the pointer
is in the list (at once when the list drops over it, as the 150+ profile RGB list does, or after a drag into a list below or
above), the combo hands tracking over: it sends the list a WM_LBUTTONDOWN. Wine's list took that as a click on the item under
the cursor, and the button-up selected that item and rolled up. The combo also forwarded its own client coordinates in that
WM_LBUTTONDOWN instead of the list's, so a list that drops ABOVE the combo closed unpicked as soon as a press-drag entered it.
Separately, closing the list without a pick -- Escape, or the program's CB_SHOWDROPDOWN(FALSE), which is what Photoshop sends
on Escape -- kept the item the hover had moved the selection to (CBRollUp(FALSE) does not restore it); Photoshop applied it.

Windows (black-box, his PC, Windows 11, comctl32 6.16, combo animation on; SendInput probes):
- combolist-probe v1/v2 (round 12/13): the hand-over happens (combo MOVE with capture=combo, list DOWN at the true point with the
  button still down, list takes the capture); the release leaves the list open, selection unchanged.
- combolist-probe3 (round 14), list over the pressed point: click, 1 px / 3 px jiggle, 200 px drag onto another item, drag and
  back: all STILL OPEN, selection unchanged, SELCHANGE x0. Only a following click (or hover then click) picks.
- combolist-probe4 (round 15): the same in EVERY case -- below-drag and above-drag (8-item list, press on the combo, drag onto
  item 4, release) STILL OPEN unchanged "comboDOWN DROPDOWN listDOWN listUP", over-drag and over-hold too. While that press is
  down only the caret follows the pointer: mid "sel 0 lbsel 0 caret 4" (below/above), caret 38 / 28 = the item under the pointer
  (over); with the button up, hovering moves selection and caret together ("sel 4 lbsel 4 caret 4"). Escape after such a hover:
  CLOSED, selection unchanged (back to item 0), SELCHANGE x0, "comboUP CLOSEUP" (below and over).
- combolist-probe5 (round 16): CB_SHOWDROPDOWN(FALSE) sent by the program after a hover (below: sel 4; over: sel 38) and without
  a hover: CLOSED, selection unchanged (item 0), SELCHANGE x0, "ENDCANCEL CLOSEUP"; Escape the same. (Wine already sends
  CBN_SELENDCANCEL before CBN_CLOSEUP on both paths.)
Revision 1 keyed on "pointer not moved"; revision 2 on "list covers the press point"; round 15 shows the rule is every press that
drops the list.

Implemented: (1) CBF_OPENPRESS is set when a press on the combo drops the list (COMBO_LButtonDown, after CBDropDown). Until that
press is released, the list takes the hand-over DOWN as capture-only, moves only its caret to the item under the pointer (on the
DOWN and on each move inside the list), and on the release -- wherever it ends -- stays open with the selection unchanged and the
capture on the list, exactly as after a release on the combo itself (COMBO_LButtonUp). The flag ends at that release (list UP or
combo UP) or any roll-up; hover tracking and the next click work as before. The hand-over DOWN carries list coordinates.
(2) Escape on a dropped list (the combo's WM_KEYDOWN) and CB_SHOWDROPDOWN(FALSE) set the list back to the selection it had when
it dropped (droppedIndex, LB_SETCURSEL, no notification) before CBRollUp(FALSE). A pick (click on an item, Enter) is untouched:
CBN_SELENDOK, item kept. A CB_SHOWDROPDOWN(FALSE) that the program sends from inside the roll-up's own CBN_SELENDOK /
CBN_SELENDCANCEL notification (Photoshop does after a pick) does not restore (CBF_INROLLUP): without that guard the restore
undid Photoshop's pick (lab, first 186pf build, 2/2 runs: item click left sRGB).

Not covered / INFERRED: (1) Other roll-ups without a pick (focus loss, a click outside the list, F4/Alt+Up) are unchanged
(Windows not measured; a click outside already restored in Wine). (2) While that first press is down and the pointer leaves the
list, Wine does not autoscroll it (Windows not measured). (3) A capture lost while that press is down leaves the flag set until
the next release in the list (one extra click). (4) Bottom clamp of a list taller than the work area: not changed (revision 1).
(5) The classic comctl32 (v5) has no combo box in this tree (user32's is used): user32's copy carries the same change.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-186pg = 186pp + this patch's comctl32_v6 + user32; desk c7a 175%, prefix at 168 dpi; "kill" = both
switches 0 on the same build):
- (probe4, probe3, v1/v2, real-pointer and Photoshop rows below were measured on revision 3's build 186pe, which differs only
  by the CB_SHOWDROPDOWN restore; probe4 and probe3 rechecked on 186pf: = Windows 1/1 each.)
- combolist-probe4: all 7 lines = Windows' (open/closed, selection, SELCHANGE count, message list, mid sel/lbsel = item 0 and
  caret = item under the pointer during the press; esc arms restore item 0) 2/2; kill 2/2: below/over drag and over-hold CLOSED
  + CHANGED, above-drag closes unpicked, both esc arms keep the hovered item. (In the full run the over-hold caret reads 60, the
  item under the nested desk's jumped SendInput cursor; the arm alone: caret 47 = item under the release, 3/3.)
- combolist-probe5: all 4 lines = Windows' 2/2 on 186pf, 1/1 on 186pg; pick arm ENDOK + item kept 2/2 on both (over-sdd mid 60 vs Windows' 38 is geometry); kill 2/2: Escape and
  CB_SHOWDROPDOWN keep the hovered item. OK path (lab-only arm: click, hover item 4, click it): ENDOK CLOSEUP SELCHANGE, item 4
  kept 2/2, kill 2/2 the same.
- combolist-probe3: all 7 RESULT lines = Windows' 2/2; kill 2/2 all CLOSED + CHANGED (item numbers differ from Windows' by geometry).
- combolist-probe v1, v2 hold 60, v2 hold 500: STILL OPEN unchanged 2/2 each (= Windows); kill CLOSED + CHANGED 1/1 each.
- Real desk pointer (fakeptr, combolist-probe2 wait), v6: click OPEN 2/2, drag 120 px + release OPEN unchanged 2/2, a second
  click picks the item under it 1/1; kill: click CLOSED 47, drag CLOSED 61. user32 combo: click OPEN 1/1, drag OPEN 1/1; kill
  drag CLOSED 61 1/1.
- Photoshop 2026 Color Settings (lab copy, real pointer; second run with WINEDEBUG=+combo): RGB one click -> list open, profile
  unchanged 2/2; press-drag 150 px and release -> open, unchanged 2/2; a click on an item then picks it and closes 2/2; Color
  Management Policies RGB (3-item list that drops below) press-drag-release onto "Convert to Working RGB" -> stays open 2/2
  (as Windows' below-drag), then Escape closes it with the policy unchanged 1/1 (screenshot checked). Kill: RGB click closes at once and changes the
  profile (Canon Cinema CLog3) 1/1, drag closes and picks 1/1; Policies drag-release picks "Convert to Working RGB" 1/1 (stock
  path, run on revision 2's build). Escape after hovering the RGB list (Photoshop closes with CB_SHOWDROPDOWN(FALSE), +combo trace): profile changed on
  revision 3 2/2. This revision: Escape after hovering keeps "sRGB IEC61966-2.1" / "North America General Purpose 2" on 186pf
  1/1 clean run (the other run's Escape step was unreadable: the window-list helper misread and the harness reopened the
  dialog) and on 186pg 1/1; one click open, drag-release open, Policies drag-release open with the policy unchanged after
  Escape: 186pf 2/2, 186pg 1/1; an item click picks on 186pg 1/1 (Fujifilm 3521XD) -- it did NOT on 186pf (field stayed sRGB,
  2/2), which is what the CBF_INROLLUP guard fixes. Kill on 186pf 2/2: RGB click closes and applies Canon Cinema CLog3, drag
  closes and applies Fujifilm 3521XD.
- Wine conformance tests (cross-built, comctl32 combo+listbox, user32 combo+listbox) identical on this build, the kill switches
  and 186pp on the same desk: 916/6485/488/3420 tests, 0 failures; 186pf = 186pp on a later desk: 916/6493/488/3420, 0 failures.
